491	/// Tauri command: forget an identity's local material WITHOUT any network step.
492	///
493	/// The escape hatch for an identity that can no longer be removed through the normal flow
494	/// because its PDS account no longer exists — deleted from another device, purged
495	/// server-side, or migrated away. In every such case the deletion endpoints can only answer
496	/// with an opaque 401: the PDS deliberately does not expose account existence, so an unknown
497	/// DID and a wrong password are indistinguishable (see
498	/// `crates/pds/src/routes/delete_account.rs`). The request/confirm flow can therefore never
499	/// make progress, and without this the identity would be stranded in the wallet forever.
500	///
501	/// This wipes the DID's Keychain material and clears any pending-removal marker. It
502	/// deliberately does NOT tombstone the did:plc: the DID may already be retired, or (the
503	/// migrate-away case) the device key is no longer a rotation key and the identity now lives
504	/// on another PDS — so "forget locally" only promises to remove the identity from THIS
505	/// device. The frontend states that plainly and gates the call behind the biometric prompt.
506	///
507	/// Returns `was_last_identity` (mirroring `RemovalOutcome`) so the UI can route back to
508	/// onboarding rather than the identity list when the wallet is now empty.
509	#[tauri::command]
510	pub fn forget_identity_locally(did: String) -> Result<bool, RemovalError> {
511	    wipe_local(&IdentityStore, &did)?;
512	    clear_removal_pending_best_effort(&did);
513	    no_identities_remain()
514	}
